skill: "settlement-reconciliation-audit"
sections[3]:
  - "# settlement-reconciliation-audit\n\nThree-way match between payment-processor settlement files, the internal payout ledger and bank statements. Use after each settlement period closes, when a payout amount looks wrong, when chargeback volume moves, or before role-cfo signs a payment approval. Classifies breaks, ages them, and drafts processor credit claims.\n\nOwner: role-treasury-banking-spec (pod-gna, finance). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"PSP settlement export per period (payout id, gross, fees, adjustments); payout ledger entries from billing-automation; bank statement lines for the settlement account; chargeback register chargebacks.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/settlement-recon.toon with matched, fee_delta and breaks[]; break-aging register with classes timing|fee|chargeback|error; agents/handoffs/settlement-breaks-accounts.toon\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Collect the three source files for one settlement period; assert all three cover the same date window before matching, otherwise stop and ask_question.\n2. Normalize amounts to the settlement currency and to minor units (cents); record every conversion rule in normalization_rules[].\n3. Match PSP payout lines to bank statement lines by payout reference id, then by amount within a tolerance window; emit matched pairs.\n4. Match the same lines to internal ledger payout entries; compute the fee delta between PSP-declared fees and ledger-booked fees.\n5. Classify every unmatched line: timing (settlement crosses the period edge), fee (delta above tolerance), chargeback (present in chargebacks.toon) or error (none of the previous).\n6. Age every break in days since the settlement date; anything older than 30 days goes to an escalation list.\n7. For fee-class breaks above the materiality threshold, draft a processor credit claim with the evidence lines attached.\n8. Recompute the period totals: PSP gross, fees, net, bank credit and ledger booking must agree to within tolerance or the report carries an unresolved flag.\n9. Write settlement-recon.toon and hand settlement-breaks-accounts.toon to role-accounts-manager for ledger correction proposals and to role-billing-payments-eng for gateway-side defects.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nledger corrections to role-accounts-manager; gateway defects to role-billing-payments-eng.\n"
